---
name: finding-group
version: 6.2.0
description: Beads formula for the fix, sanity and QA tasks of one blocking finding, attached under its sprint container. bead-groups supplies every variable.
format: toml
required_variables:
  - parent
  - ref
  - finding_ref
  - round
  - severity
  - reviewer
  - finding_title
  - remedy
  - filed_by
  - found_at_commit
  - requirements
  - adrs
  - phase
  - sprint
  - stack
  - difficulty
  - branch
  - worktree
  - pr_target
  - priority
  - edge_option
  - stack_bead
  - checked_title
  - phase_feature
  - lint_command
  - policy_path
  - max_sanity_rounds
defaults:
  found_on_layer: ""
  has_found_on_layer: false
---
{#
sc-compose beads formula (sc-compose/beads/v1, ADR-0021): the fix group of one
blocking finding, poured as siblings directly under the sprint container
(Rand, 2026-10-03): fix <- sanity <- qa, the same shape as the sprint's
dev <- sanity <- qa. The fix bead is the dev's assigned task and carries the
finding (finding_ref, severity, filing reviewer, remedy); there is no
separate finding bead for a blocking finding. Poured ids are
<sprint>.<finding_ref>-r<round>-<step>. The sprint cannot close while any
poured group bead is open. Important and minor findings are not poured: QA
files them as plain finding beads against the phase or feature.

No step sets an assignee: every poured bead carries `difficulty` and the lead
picks the agent at dispatch.

Closers:
  fix     the dev closes it when the fix is committed
  sanity  dev-sanity closes it on PASS only; on FAIL it reopens the fix
          bead and leaves sanity open, which re-blocks sanity through its
          `needs fix` edge
  qa      quality-mgr closes it, only after pouring the fix
          groups of the blocking findings it raised (bead-groups refuses to
          pour a group once the QA bead named in `filed_by` is closed) and
          filing its important and minor findings

`{{{ ... }}}` are compose variables, baked at render time (see
sprint-group.formula.toml.j2). round and priority must be integers;
requirements and adrs are lists of ids.

Compose variables (bead-groups fills them from the findings file, the sprint
container and the repository configuration):
  parent         the attach parent: the sprint container
  ref            attach reference, "<finding_ref>-r<round>"
  finding_ref, round, severity, reviewer, remedy, finding_title, filed_by
  found_at_commit, requirements, adrs
  found_on_layer  optional provenance copied from the checked bead
  phase, sprint, stack, difficulty, priority
  stack_bead, checked_title, phase_feature, lint_command, policy_path,
  max_sanity_rounds
                 the close fields (close_fields.POURED) every step carries, so
                 its close reads no other bead; max_sanity_rounds is bare
  edge_option    E1 option "C" (default), "B" or "A", as in sprint-group
#}
formula = "finding-group"
description = "Fix of blocking finding {{{ finding_ref }}}, round {{{ round }}}, in sprint {{{ sprint }}}."
version = 6
type = "workflow"

[[steps]]
id = "fix"
title = "{{{ sprint }}}: fix {{{ finding_ref }}}: {{{ finding_title }}}"
description = "Fix blocking finding {{{ finding_ref }}} (round {{{ round }}}), filed by {{{ reviewer }}} in {{{ filed_by }}}.\n\nRemedy: {{{ remedy }}}\n\nCommit the fix on the sprint's stack, then close this bead. A dev-sanity check and the filing reviewer's verification follow.\n\n## Deliverables\n1. {{{ remedy }}}"
type = "task"
priority = {{{ priority }}}
labels = ["phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stack:{{{ stack }}}", "stage:fix"]

[steps.metadata]
role = "fix"
phase = "{{{ phase }}}"
sprint = "{{{ sprint }}}"
stack = "{{{ stack }}}"
round = {{{ round }}}
difficulty = "{{{ difficulty }}}"
branch = "{{{ branch }}}"
worktree = "{{{ worktree }}}"
pr_target = "{{{ pr_target }}}"
sprint_bead = "{{{ parent }}}"
finding_ref = "{{{ finding_ref }}}"
severity = "{{{ severity }}}"
reviewer = "{{{ reviewer }}}"
remedy = "{{{ remedy }}}"
filed_by = "{{{ filed_by }}}"
found_at_commit = "{{{ found_at_commit }}}"
{% if has_found_on_layer %}found_on_layer = {{{ found_on_layer | tojson }}}
{% endif %}
requirements = [{% for r in requirements %}"{{{ r }}}"{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}]
adrs = [{% for r in adrs %}"{{{ r }}}"{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}]
checked_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-fix"
stack_bead = "{{{ stack_bead }}}"
base = "{{{ pr_target }}}"
checked_title = "{{{ checked_title }}}"
sanity_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-sanity"
qa_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-qa"
phase_feature = "{{{ phase_feature }}}"
lint_command = "{{{ lint_command }}}"
policy_path = "{{{ policy_path }}}"
max_sanity_rounds = {{{ max_sanity_rounds }}}
{% if edge_option != "A" %}

[[steps]]
id = "sanity"
title = "{{{ sprint }}}: sanity check of the fix of {{{ finding_ref }}}"
description = "Sanity check of {{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-fix: each numbered deliverable is written and lint passes. This is not QA. Close on PASS only; on FAIL reopen the fix bead and leave this bead open."
type = "task"
priority = {{{ priority }}}
labels = ["phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stack:{{{ stack }}}", "stage:dev-sanity"]
{% if edge_option == "C" %}needs = ["fix"]
{% endif %}
[steps.metadata]
role = "sanity"
phase = "{{{ phase }}}"
sprint = "{{{ sprint }}}"
stack = "{{{ stack }}}"
sprint_bead = "{{{ parent }}}"
checked_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-fix"
stack_bead = "{{{ stack_bead }}}"
base = "{{{ pr_target }}}"
checked_title = "{{{ checked_title }}}"
sanity_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-sanity"
qa_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-qa"
phase_feature = "{{{ phase_feature }}}"
lint_command = "{{{ lint_command }}}"
policy_path = "{{{ policy_path }}}"
max_sanity_rounds = {{{ max_sanity_rounds }}}
dev_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-fix"
difficulty = "{{{ difficulty }}}"
branch = "{{{ branch }}}"
worktree = "{{{ worktree }}}"
pr_target = "{{{ pr_target }}}"

[[steps]]
id = "qa"
title = "{{{ sprint }}}: verify the fix of {{{ finding_ref }}}"
description = "Fix verification of {{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-fix for finding {{{ finding_ref }}}, by its filing reviewer {{{ reviewer }}} only, after its sanity check passes."
type = "task"
priority = {{{ priority }}}
labels = ["phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stack:{{{ stack }}}", "stage:qa"]
needs = ["sanity"]

[steps.metadata]
role = "qa"
phase = "{{{ phase }}}"
sprint = "{{{ sprint }}}"
stack = "{{{ stack }}}"
round = {{{ round }}}
difficulty = "{{{ difficulty }}}"
branch = "{{{ branch }}}"
worktree = "{{{ worktree }}}"
pr_target = "{{{ pr_target }}}"
checked_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-fix"
finding_ref = "{{{ finding_ref }}}"
reviewer = "{{{ reviewer }}}"
reviewers_round1 = ["{{{ reviewer }}}"]
sprint_bead = "{{{ parent }}}"
stack_bead = "{{{ stack_bead }}}"
base = "{{{ pr_target }}}"
checked_title = "{{{ checked_title }}}"
sanity_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-sanity"
qa_bead = "{{{ parent }}}.{{{ ref }}}-qa"
phase_feature = "{{{ phase_feature }}}"
lint_command = "{{{ lint_command }}}"
policy_path = "{{{ policy_path }}}"
max_sanity_rounds = {{{ max_sanity_rounds }}}
{% endif %}
